mit_sha":"f5679218b635a9c75fb74f916e60c9f3e6ae5104","position":"1787381367573589001-5798edd0-9afc-4de3-8cf8-4b6905b558f6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"66cad916f597e95ab1cb8c18d030c7c46c1a6ff8cb5c658879fa54e178e96254","event_uuid":"9657f0c1-0dba-48e2-8483-f67b5d6b61b2","position":{"commit_sha":"264870a2eef9160f71bdb6170fa44c47625fdc5c","position":"1787381387582554001-9657f0c1-0dba-48e2-8483-f67b5d6b61b2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787377461405889001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"fe09253b-72cc-4cca-8af1-f2fb92c1385d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d893-e003-0539-47fc"}],"description":"## Discovered from\n\nCI run 32553346737 on Gerrit change 2065 (ticket d893-e003-0539-47fc): pytest (ubuntu-latest,\npy3.12) failed tests/unit/test_plan_review.py::test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes\nwith 'rebar-version: 0.12.0 (f5fb6e45-dirty)' != 'rebar-version: 0.12.0 (f5fb6e45)' — the -dirty\nsuffix flipped BETWEEN two build_manifest calls inside one test. The same test passes locally.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed by deterministic reproduction)\n\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:497 stamps every manifest with\n`_signing.gate_code_version()`, which shells `git status --porcelain` on the rebar source\ncheckout PER CALL (src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py:_gate_commit_sha). Two byte-equality tests\ncompare manifests built by SEPARATE calls:\n\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review.py:965-966 (test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py:79 (equality of two build_manifest outputs)\n\nUnder pytest-xdist another worker that transiently creates/removes a file in the checkout\n(or any concurrent writer) flips the dirty-state between the calls, so the assertion compares\nracy live-git provenance rather than the file-scope/pins contract under test. Reproduced\ndeterministically: creating a scratch file in the checkout between the two calls makes the\nequality fail with exactly the CI diff.\n\n## Approach\n\nPin the provenance in the affected test: monkeypatch `rebar.signing.gate_code_version` to a\nconstant in test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes — manifest.py binds\n`from rebar import signing as _signing` (manifest.py:475) and calls\n`_signing.gate_code_version()` at call time (manifest.py:497), so pinning the attribute on the\n`rebar.signing` facade module is what the call site actually resolves through; no production\ncode changes. This is the exact pattern the OTHER byte-equality test already uses:\ntests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py::test_no_pins_preserves_legacy_manifest_bytes already\nmonkeypatches `rebar.signing.gate_code_version` to a constant around its line-79 equality, A second unpinned site exists in the same class:\ntests/unit/test_gate_engine_cutover.py::test_manifest_is_deterministic_and_path_independent\nbyte-compares separately-built manifests (m1 == m2 at lines 48-50, and the m3 comparison after\nit) with no gate_code_version pin — pin it the same way. After this fix every manifest\nbyte-equality test in the repo is pinned and the flake class is closed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes pins\n      `rebar.signing.gate_code_version` (monkeypatch, like\n      test_no_pins_preserves_legacy_manifest_bytes) and passes even when a file is created in\n      the checkout between its build_manifest calls — verified by running the test with the\n      reproduction interleaving.\n- [ ] test_manifest_is_deterministic_and_path_independent (tests/unit/test_gate_engine_cutover.py)\n      pins `rebar.signing.gate_code_version` the same way around its manifest equalities.\n- [ ] A repo grep shows no remaining test byte-compares two separately-built manifests without\n      pinning gate_code_version (tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py:79 is already pinned by\n      its enclosing test test_no_pins_preserves_legacy_manifest_bytes).\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review.py","reason":"Pin rebar.signing.gate_code_version via monkeypatch in test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes so the byte-equality asserts the file-scope contract, not racy live-git dirty state (mirrors the pin already in test_plan_material_pins.py)."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_engine_cutover.py","reason":"Same flake class: pin rebar.signing.gate_code_version in test_manifest_is_deterministic_and_path_independent around its m1/m2/m3 byte-equalities."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b44c-2a74-2daf-4b59","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Manifest byte-equality tests sample live git dirty-state and flake under xdist","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f28b20c8-77e3-4a1e-9833-63dd166def12","fe09253b-72cc-4cca-8af1-f2fb92c1385d","03148c81-acca-41f9-8d50-226f02e3250e","5d2e1393-38ab-4186-b95a-e1940b301975","294eac4d-6fa0-42a6-b8bc-91182c3bc15e","9e0715b3-210b-4d91-bfc0-87d2766f9e81","5798edd0-9afc-4de3-8cf8-4b6905b558f6","9657f0c1-0dba-48e2-8483-f67b5d6b61b2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787381387582554002,"uuid":"0253f55c-8089-46d1-ac5e-b9b6611a5ceb"}